0..56 Comment "//! `file-base` defines the shared linear file protocol."
57..60 Comment "//!"
61..139 Comment "//! A holder closes one descriptor. A move delegates that duty. The move twins"
140..220 Comment "//! refuse a repeated move or a post-move close as `UsedAfterClose`. They refuse"
221..263 Comment "//! an unclosed handle as `LinearResidue`."
264..267 Comment "//!"
268..347 Comment "//! Each moves source imports `File`. It uses `Handle`, `Closer`, `Writer`, and"
348..359 Comment "//! `line`."
360..363 Comment "//!"
364..420 Comment "//! The protocol follows POSIX `open(2)` and `close(2)`."
421..475 Comment "//! A handle is the linear resident of a forked owner."
476..579 Comment "//! - cites: [Honda-1998-language_primitives_type_discipline_structured_communicationbased_programming]"
580..583 Comment "//!"
584..832 Comment "//! [Honda-1998-language_primitives_type_discipline_structured_communicationbased_programming]: https://doi.org/10.1007/BFb0053567 \"Honda, Vasconcelos and Kubo, Language Primitives and Type Discipline for Structured Communication-Based Programming\""
834..907 Comment "/// `File` defines a handle protocol with a closer, a writer, and a line."
